<http://data.silknow.org/object/8ef1c183-879f-3c43-9f12-6dddfc92e864>
        a                 ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment      "Woman's tulle cap, England, ca. 1880"@en , "Woman's cap of white tulle trimmed with rows of pleated silk gauze frills. There is a band of swansdown variegated with black fronds, and on the crown is a mount of black and white artificial flowers and a jet spray. There are black grosgrain ribbons pinned to the front. The cap is wired into a pointed oval shape, and would have been worn on the crown of the head."@en ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note  "Woman's tulle cap, England, ca. 1880"@en , "Woman's cap of white tulle trimmed with rows of pleated silk gauze frills. There is a band of swansdown variegated with black fronds, and on the crown is a mount of black and white artificial flowers and a jet spray. There are black grosgrain ribbons pinned to the front. The cap is wired into a pointed oval shape, and would have been worn on the crown of the head."@en ;
        dc:identifier     "T.851-1974" ;
        <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#sameAs>
                <https://collections.vam.ac.uk/item/O353593> .

